# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Processed before the SPA fallback.

# WEB-UX-016: canonical Visitor Guide is /visitors-guide. The pSEO
# /things-to-do/tourists page duplicated that concept — 301 to the canonical.
/things-to-do/tourists  /visitors-guide  301

# WEB-SEO-007: /weekend and /events/this-weekend targeted the same query.
# /events/this-weekend is the canonical one — it declares its own canonical URL,
# emits EventListJsonLd and carries FAQ content, none of which /weekend did.
# The route in App.tsx stays for now: per the Backward Compatibility rules in
# CLAUDE.md a public route needs its 301 in place for at least one release
# cycle before the route itself is removed.
/weekend  /events/this-weekend  301

# WEB-SEO-019: two restaurants existed twice at the same address. The row that
# Google had indexed was the one with the -2 slug in both cases - the clean
# slugs had zero impressions in the whole GSC window - so the duplicate that
# was removed is the clean-slugged one, and these keep its URL alive.
# Renaming the survivor instead would have moved a URL that ranks at position
# 11.9 with 388 impressions, which is the one thing worth not doing here.
/restaurants/daves-hot-chicken   /restaurants/daves-hot-chicken-2   301
/restaurants/outback-steakhouse  /restaurants/outback-steakhouse-2  301
